  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) has finalized plans to execute the prison sentences of three former officials from the Directorate General of Customs and Excise. This follows court verdicts that have achieved a permanent legal status, or 'inkrah.' The convicted individuals, named as Rizal, Sisprian, and Orlando, were handed prison terms ranging from six to nine years. These developments conclude the legal process regarding their involvement in a corruption case. Concurrently, the anti-corruption body continues to investigate other areas of potential misconduct within the customs sector, including recent inquiries regarding container seizures at Tanjung Emas and ongoing investigations involving the head of the Semarang Customs office. The enforcement of these prison sentences marks a significant milestone in the broader efforts to address corruption within Indonesia's financial and customs institutions.",
